WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.036
-Our next guest is a very funny
actress and comedian

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:05.572
you know from shows
such as "Vice Principals"

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:06.672
and "The Last OG."

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:08.908
She's starring
in the second season

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:10.310
of "The Righteous Gemstones."

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:13.746
New episodes are available
Sundays on HBO and HBO Max.

00:00:13.746 --> 00:00:14.914
Let's take a look.

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:18.184
-BJ, I'm saying
something nice right now.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:21.520
-You're right.
I'm sorry.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.823
This is an exciting day.
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:26.259
Let's not ruin it.
-The only ones who can ruin it

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:28.594
are the ones
who try to hold us back.

00:00:28.594 --> 00:00:30.129
Like your family.

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:32.565
-Nobody can hold us back.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:35.502
Not when I'm wearing this.

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:38.470
-Yeah, boy!

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:40.940
Yeah, shake that cake!

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.277
-Please welcome back to the show
our friend Edi Patterson.

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:46.279
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:56.289 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:59.124 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:59.124 --> 00:01:00.760
Hi, Edi!
-Hi, Seth.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:01.761
-Welcome back.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.863
Congratulations on season 2.
-Thanks.

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:05.397
-Congratulations
on your outfits.

00:01:05.397 --> 00:01:07.734
You really get to wear
some fantastic outfits.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:11.237
-Yeah, they really go for it
with Judy's outfits.

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:13.439
-Do you get excited when you --
-Shout-out to Sarah Trost.

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:14.707
-Sorry.
Who's the shout-out to?

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:17.610
-Sarah Trost, our genius
of a costume designer.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:18.744
-Yes, she's done --

00:01:18.744 --> 00:01:20.446
Do you get excited
when you see the outfits?

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:24.150
-I get really excited
because I would say,

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.586
9 times out of 10,
I've got two categories,

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:29.622
and it's either, like,
mm, church chic

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:32.592
or ice skater.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:34.961
Like, what an ice skater
would wear to go, like,

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.562
"I'm gonna get crazy today."

00:01:36.562 --> 00:01:37.730
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.164
-You talked,
last time you were here,

00:01:39.164 --> 00:01:41.601
you grew up in Texas, you
grew up in a religious family.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:45.604
-Yeah.
-And you did not sort of

00:01:45.604 --> 00:01:47.673
suggest to your mom
that she watch season 1.

00:01:47.673 --> 00:01:49.975
Or, maybe your mom wasn't
suggesting it to other people.

00:01:49.975 --> 00:01:52.779
-Yeah, my mom was very into it.
But she probably,

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:55.181
I said,
wasn't telling people at church.

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:57.783
-Okay, gotcha.
-Now that's changed.

00:01:57.783 --> 00:01:59.285
-Oh, that's great.
-Yeah.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:01.621
And if they're not into it,
they can hit the bricks...

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:02.655
-All right.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.090
-...as far as
my mom's concerned.

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:05.724
-I'm very happy that your mom
is being supportive of this.

00:02:05.724 --> 00:02:06.992
-My mom's always
been supportive of it.

00:02:06.992 --> 00:02:08.294
-Right.
-She just knew, like,

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.296
"Maybe some people,
don't talk to them about it."

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.231
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:16.469
But the weird thing is,
I just was with her recently,

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:18.804
and everyone she talks to
about it and everyone

00:02:18.804 --> 00:02:21.740
who's sort of close to us
is, like, fully on board.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.810
They're, like,
real into the "Gemstones."

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:27.045
They're real into
how nasty Judy is.

00:02:27.045 --> 00:02:30.783
Even if they're real churchy,
they're down to clown.

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.919
But the weird thing
about going home is, like --

00:02:33.919 --> 00:02:35.221
There's -- I don't know.

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:39.458
There can be this aspect
of, like, super, super excited

00:02:39.458 --> 00:02:41.427
from people, because they
know how hard you've worked,

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:44.830
or this weird thing where
they're like -- I don't know --

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:48.067
you almost get humbled
because they --

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:50.336
I just was there,
and this dude we kind of know

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:52.605
from growing up came up to me.

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:56.575
And he was like, "Hmm.
Hey, I, uh..."

00:02:56.575 --> 00:02:59.411
kind of with a sad voice
or disappointed voice --

00:02:59.411 --> 00:03:00.880
"...haven't seen you
on anything."

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.782
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.183
"How's --
How's it all going?

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:05.751
I haven't seen you on anything."

00:03:05.751 --> 00:03:08.554
And I was like,
"Um, it's going great.

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:11.490
I -- yeah, I don't know
what to tell you, dude.

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:14.159
I'm mostly just busy
working on the show that I'm on

00:03:14.159 --> 00:03:15.828
and that I write for.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.530
Sorry I'm not on baseball."

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.631
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.631 --> 00:03:21.400
And I'm, like, sitting there,
getting pissed,

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.336
and I'm thinking like,
"Man, I know for a fact

00:03:24.336 --> 00:03:27.039
you had a girlfriend --
a grown-woman girlfriend --

00:03:27.039 --> 00:03:28.808
who moved out not too long ago,

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:31.744
who took all your furniture
while you were somewhere else.

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.579
And I know you've
been living with one chair

00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:36.416
in your house
for at least a few months."

00:03:36.416 --> 00:03:37.583
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:40.152
"And not because
you can't go buy other chairs.

00:03:40.152 --> 00:03:42.254
Just because you're that dude.

00:03:42.254 --> 00:03:43.923
So, like, don't tell me like,

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:45.358
'I haven't seen you
in anything.'"

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:47.159
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:49.362
-"You got to have a second chair
before you come to me."

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:50.730
-Yeah.
Yeah, for real!

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.398
Like, have a second chair
before you're going to be

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:54.967
disappointed in my life.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:57.336
-Did you --
Did you find out early

00:03:57.336 --> 00:04:00.405
in your life in Texas
that comedy was a skill you had?

00:04:00.405 --> 00:04:01.941
Were you appreciated?

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:05.177
-Yeah, well, I was definitely
appreciated in my house

00:04:05.177 --> 00:04:07.513
and then with my friends.

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:09.282
And I would try --

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:10.650
Yeah, I would definitely
try things.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.551
I went through definitely
a phase where, like,

00:04:12.551 --> 00:04:13.820
everything funny to me

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:15.721
was acting like things
I'd already seen.

00:04:15.721 --> 00:04:18.725
So there's, like,
probably a thousand VHS tapes

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:21.860
of me being Pat from "SNL."
-Right.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:23.763
-There's probably
a thousand VHS tapes

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:25.598
of me being Fire Marshall Bill
and like --

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:26.999
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.999 --> 00:04:30.202
But I would try things I had
discovered on my own in my room,

00:04:30.202 --> 00:04:31.670
and then I would do them
with them.

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:34.206
Like, there's a classic one --

00:04:34.206 --> 00:04:36.376
I don't know why
I think you can do this, but...

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:38.644
-I don't think I can.
I definitely can't.

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:39.912
I don't know
why you thought I could.

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:41.113
But tell everybody
what you're about to do.

00:04:41.113 --> 00:04:42.648
-I can talk
with my mouth closed,

00:04:42.648 --> 00:04:44.283
and this was a thing
I discovered

00:04:44.283 --> 00:04:45.785
trying to be funny
for my friends.

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:50.255
-Okay.
-And it started from, like --

00:04:50.255 --> 00:04:52.625
Like, at a slumber party,

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:54.427
screaming so parents
couldn't hear.

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:57.263
Like, we're up,
screwing around or whatever,

00:04:57.263 --> 00:04:59.265
and I screamed into a pillow,
and I went,

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:01.634
"Oh, I bet that I could do that
inside my mouth.

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:04.003
Oh, and I bet
I can say sentences."

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:06.071
[ Laughter ]
-Okay. Well, I mean --

00:05:06.071 --> 00:05:08.373
I don't know what
to tell you other than show us.

00:05:08.373 --> 00:05:10.610
-I thought you could do this.
-I definitely can't do --

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:13.912
-But it's just that I can --

00:05:13.912 --> 00:05:16.315
I can really just, like, say...

00:05:16.315 --> 00:05:18.551
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:21.554
I can say anything
that I would normally say.

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:23.055
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.055 --> 00:05:25.891
But it's -- it's creepy
because it's almost like

00:05:25.891 --> 00:05:27.627
there's someone inside of me.

00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:29.862
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:34.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
-That's...

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:36.536
I mean...

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:39.238
That was exactly what you said
you were gonna do,

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:41.407
and I still couldn't expect it
to be like that.

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:43.542
-Yeah, it's confusing.
It's weird.

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:44.944
-Mm -- Mm-mm...

00:05:44.944 --> 00:05:46.979
-You got to get
some air in there, yeah.

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:48.514
-Mm -- Mm.
Nope.

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:51.083
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:54.320
That was -- That was almost
a level of some --

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:56.889
like, a trait somebody
might have in a horror film.

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:59.225
You --
But you were --

00:05:59.225 --> 00:06:00.393
Who introduced you to horror?

00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:01.527
Because I know
that was something you love.

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:04.196
-My dad loved horror movies.
-Okay.

00:06:04.196 --> 00:06:06.699
-And as a result, my sister
and I loved horror movies.

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:09.001
-That's great.
-Yeah. Way too young.

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:10.836
-Okay.
-Like, really young.

00:06:10.836 --> 00:06:14.073
Like...probably saw
"The Shining" when I was 8.

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:16.876
-Yeah, that's too young.
-But like --

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:19.545
My brain was
so weirdly altered from it

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:21.547
that when normal things
would happen in real life,

00:06:21.547 --> 00:06:22.948
I would think,

00:06:22.948 --> 00:06:25.951
"Oh, something supernatural's
happening -- to me."

00:06:25.951 --> 00:06:27.754
-Okay.
-"This is happening."

00:06:27.754 --> 00:06:29.955
-This is something that would
happen to you at what ages?

00:06:29.955 --> 00:06:32.358
-Like --
Oh, the one I'm thinking of

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:34.493
right now, I was probably 17.
-Okay.

00:06:34.493 --> 00:06:35.894
-Not a child.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:06:35.894 --> 00:06:38.464
-Like --
A child but not a child.

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:39.698
Closer to an adult.

00:06:39.698 --> 00:06:43.402
But I was at my grandmom's
in La Grange, Texas.

00:06:43.402 --> 00:06:47.105
And I had gone for a run.
It was just getting dusk.

00:06:47.105 --> 00:06:49.775
And, like, at the top
of every hill where she lived,

00:06:49.775 --> 00:06:51.510
there was a light.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:54.213
And so you could see something
far away on the hill,

00:06:54.213 --> 00:06:55.781
but when you ran,
you couldn't see it.

00:06:55.781 --> 00:06:58.117
Anyway, out for a run.

00:06:58.117 --> 00:07:01.520
I see this shape coming
over the road.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:04.690
I'm like, "Oh, okay.
Yeah, cool, somebody running."

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.626
And then I turn back around,

00:07:06.626 --> 00:07:11.363
and it's exponentially closer
than it was.

00:07:11.363 --> 00:07:14.667
Like, way closer
than a human being could be.

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:15.935
-Yeah.
-But my brain,

00:07:15.935 --> 00:07:20.406
because of horror movies,
goes, "Demon. Get inside."

00:07:20.406 --> 00:07:21.774
Fully thought it was a demon.

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:24.277
Ran to my grandmom's house.

00:07:24.277 --> 00:07:25.644
Locked the door.

00:07:25.644 --> 00:07:28.581
She had these sort of, like,
full windows in the front,

00:07:28.581 --> 00:07:30.983
like, floor-to-ceiling
windows in the front

00:07:30.983 --> 00:07:32.418
and those vertical blinds.

00:07:32.418 --> 00:07:34.453
And I remember crouching
on the floor, shaking,

00:07:34.453 --> 00:07:36.721
looking out the blinds,
waiting for a demon

00:07:36.721 --> 00:07:38.925
to come past on the road.

00:07:38.925 --> 00:07:40.693
And my mom and my grandmom
were like,

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:42.695
"What are you doing
on the ground?"

00:07:42.695 --> 00:07:44.797
And I'm like,
"Oh, it's not a big deal.

00:07:44.797 --> 00:07:47.533
I just -- I don't want to
talk about it right now."

00:07:47.533 --> 00:07:49.368
And so I'm looking, looking.

00:07:49.368 --> 00:07:52.170
The weirdest thing is, I fully
thought a demon would come by,

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:55.173
and it was some dude
on a 10-speed, like,

00:07:55.173 --> 00:07:56.642
doing that with no hands.

00:07:56.642 --> 00:08:00.078
[ Laughter ]

00:08:00.078 --> 00:08:02.581
Going faster than a human would.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:08:02.581 --> 00:08:04.183
With a bike,
you would go faster, yeah.

00:08:04.183 --> 00:08:06.285
-The first earthquake
I ever experienced in L.A.,

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:09.956
I really thought, "Here we go --
dimensional shift."

00:08:09.956 --> 00:08:12.558
[ Laughter ]

00:08:12.558 --> 00:08:14.360
'Cause the floor was, like,
rolling, and I'm like,

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:15.961
"Okay, it's happening.
This is, like,

00:08:15.961 --> 00:08:18.664
dimensional shift, Rapture,
one of those, okay."

00:08:18.664 --> 00:08:19.999
[ Laughter ]

00:08:19.999 --> 00:08:21.833
-Then are you deeply relieved
when you find out

00:08:21.833 --> 00:08:23.335
that it's something
like an earthquake?

00:08:23.335 --> 00:08:24.970
-Always!
-Okay, good.

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:26.305
-Yes.
-There's no part of you

00:08:26.305 --> 00:08:27.607
that's a little bummed
it wasn't a demon?

00:08:27.607 --> 00:08:29.241
-No, I don't want it.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:08:29.241 --> 00:08:31.710
-No, I don't -- I don't want it.
-That is good to hear.

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:34.346
-Yeah, I don't want it.
I do not want it.

00:08:34.346 --> 00:08:35.714
-You seem like
you're a little on the fence.

00:08:35.714 --> 00:08:37.115
-No, I'm not on the fence!

00:08:37.115 --> 00:08:39.651
I'm thinking about this time
that I woke up in the night

00:08:39.651 --> 00:08:41.554
and looked
to the side of my bed --

00:08:41.554 --> 00:08:43.689
Wow. We're really
getting into it now --

00:08:43.689 --> 00:08:45.391
and there was, like,
a shape by my bed.

00:08:45.391 --> 00:08:48.460
-Uh-huh.
-Like, a very dark shape.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:52.765
And I was half asleep.
In my brain, I went, "Scare it."

00:08:52.765 --> 00:08:54.133
[ Laughter ]

00:08:54.133 --> 00:08:58.970
And so from the depths
of my sleep, I went, "Ooohhhh!"

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:02.240
Like, really, really deep.
And Dan, my husband, goes,

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:04.944
"Um...
What's happening?"

00:09:04.944 --> 00:09:07.279
And I was like,
"There was this thing.

00:09:07.279 --> 00:09:09.748
I had to scare it --
I had to scare it back to Hell,"

00:09:09.748 --> 00:09:11.450
or, you know, whatever.

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:13.085
So we're laying there,
it's silent,

00:09:13.085 --> 00:09:17.256
and Dan goes, "Um, why'd you
scream so deep like that?"

00:09:17.256 --> 00:09:19.258
[ Laughter ]

00:09:19.258 --> 00:09:21.260
And then, I'm kind of scared
that he's saying that,

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:23.529
'cause I don't totally know
how I sounded.

00:09:23.529 --> 00:09:25.698
And he's like, "Yeah,
it was really, really deep."

00:09:25.698 --> 00:09:26.865
And I was like,
"Well, I was trying to scare it.

00:09:26.865 --> 00:09:28.067
I don't -- I don't know."

00:09:28.067 --> 00:09:30.369
And then,
beat, beat, beat, he goes,

00:09:30.369 --> 00:09:32.437
"It sounded kind of like
you were possessed."

00:09:32.437 --> 00:09:36.709
[ Laughter ]
And I'm like, "Great, dude!"

00:09:36.709 --> 00:09:40.312
-Well, I mean, no offense,
but I feel like

00:09:40.312 --> 00:09:42.081
Dan had the scarier night.

00:09:42.081 --> 00:09:46.184
[ Laughter ]
-Okay, fair, fair, fair.

00:09:46.184 --> 00:09:47.586
-Hey, thank you so much
for being here.

00:09:47.586 --> 00:09:49.955
Congrats again.
-Thanks.

00:09:49.955 --> 00:09:51.557
-Edi Patterson, everybody.

00:09:51.557 --> 00:09:54.226
New episodes of
"The Righteous Gemstones."

00:09:54.226 --> 00:09:55.961
Will you actually
say it real quick?

00:09:55.961 --> 00:09:58.363
-Yeah, of course.
-Will you say that

00:09:58.363 --> 00:10:00.365
they're available Sundays
on HBO and HBO Max

00:10:00.365 --> 00:10:04.870
with your mouth closed?
-Yes.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:08.841
Available Sundays
on HBO and HBO Max.

00:10:08.841 --> 00:10:10.042
[ Laughter ]

00:10:10.042 --> 00:10:12.411
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night"!

